    "value": " *Default State*\n\n# Given the cart contains one or more items with no errors on a domestic storefront, when the cart summary component renders, then the button group displays in the following order: Checkout CTA (primary, full-width black button), Apple Pay Express button (outlined), Google Pay Express button (outlined).\n\n*International*\n\n# Given a Shopper is on an international storefront, when the button group renders, then Apple Pay and Google Pay Express buttons are not displayed and the content above the Checkout CTA shifts up to fill the space with no white gap.\n\n*Error States*\n\n# Given the cart contains an error condition (fully OOS, partially OOS, unavailable item, or quantity error requiring customer action), when the error state renders, then the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay and Google Pay Express buttons remain visually enabled but are blocked at backend level from processing\n# Given a Shopper resolves all error conditions in the cart, when the last error is resolved, then the Checkout CTA, Apple Pay Express, and Google Pay Express buttons can successfully process — the backend block is removed and the Shopper can proceed\n\n*Checkout Routing*\n\n# Given a Shopper on a domestic storefront clicks the Checkout CTA regardless of authentication status, when the action is triggered, then they are taken directly to checkout.\n# Given a Guest Shopper on an international storefront clicks the Checkout CTA, when the action is triggered, then they are directed to an intermediate login page before being handed off to Global-e (see SFCC-880).\n# Given an Authenticated Shopper on an international storefront clicks the Checkout CTA, when the action is triggered, then they are taken directly to the Global-e checkout flow without an intermediate login step (see SFCC-63).\n\n*Responsive*\n\n# Given a Shopper views the button group on any device, when it renders, then all buttons display correctly and are fully interactive across desktop, tablet, and mobile breakpoints in line with Figma specifications."
